## 4. Additional Fix: Introduce WAIT Action Type

The current prompt uses HOLD for two distinct situations that should be communicated differently:

- **HOLD** — you own this stock, keep it
- **HOLD** (misused) — you do not own this stock, but the entry is deferred

This creates confusion. A user seeing HOLD on LITE (which they do not own) reasonably expects it means they have a position.

**Fix**: Add a WAIT action type to the response format.

| Action type | Meaning |
|---|---|
| BUY | Enter or add to a position |
| SELL | Exit or reduce a position |
| HOLD | You own this stock — keep it as-is |
| WAIT | You do not own this stock — entry deferred, conditions not yet right |

---

## 5. What Does Not Change

- 30-day hold and FIFO enforcement
- Hard stop-loss at -10% and profit target at +20%
- Monthly budget handling (per CR008)
- Sequential cash flow calculation
- Material events deep analysis requirement
- Narrative tracking and update format
- JSON response format — unchanged except addition of WAIT type
- Earnings calendar rules (no buy within 7 days, no sell within 3 days)

---

## 6. Success Criteria

| Scenario | Expected Advisor Behaviour |
|---|---|
| Stock down due to macro, thesis intact, RSI oversold | Reasons through averaging down opportunity; recommends BUY if risk/reward favorable |
| Stock down due to earnings miss + rank slip | Identifies 2+ thesis-breaking signals; recommends EXIT when eligible |
| Stock down due to macro, rank unchanged, no news | Holds position; explains macro vs stock-specific distinction explicitly |
| Better opportunity available but current holding thesis intact | Does not swap; explains conviction in current holding |
| Better opportunity available AND current holding rank slipped + loss | Considers swap; weighs opportunity cost explicitly |
| Watchlist stock ranked #3, entry favorable but cash needed as buffer | Returns WAIT (not HOLD); explains deferral reason clearly |
| NVDA post-earnings beat, RSI 37, P&L -5%, macro-driven weakness | Recommends averaging down with explicit risk/reward reasoning |

---

## 7. Out of Scope

- No changes to how portfolio cash balance is tracked or updated
- No changes to the stock ranking algorithm or fundamental scoring
- No new data inputs added to the prompt
- No changes to the CLI or user interface
- This is a prompt architecture change only — no application code changes required